# Coordinator-set inputs for runtime/scripts/verify-gate.sh
# Copy to .env locally if you want; .env is gitignored. Never put secrets here.
# Full semantics: docs/verify-gate.md
# Every input below also reads as OPEN_FLEET_<same suffix> (ORCA_MANIFEST also as
# OPEN_FLEET_GATE_MANIFEST or OPEN_FLEET_MANIFEST). Set one spelling: when two are set and
# disagree, the gate BLOCKS (exit 2) rather than letting one silently win.

# Path to the unit's evidence manifest JSON (required on TaskCompleted)
# ORCA_MANIFEST=

# Frozen contract path@ref and its sha256 (required for a sound scope check)
# ORCA_CONTRACT_SOURCE=
# ORCA_CONTRACT_DIGEST=

# owner/name for the independent GitHub review lookup (optional; inferred from origin)
# ORCA_REPO=

# Ancestry-check base branch / a unit symbol to grep on it (optional)
# ORCA_BASE=
# ORCA_SYMBOL=

# mutation | report-only | planning  (missing/unknown => mutation)
# ORCA_UNIT_CLASS=

# Switch (on: 1|true|yes|on · off: unset|0|false|no|off · anything else BLOCKS) to forward
# --execute-nc: the negative control is EXECUTED, not read — applied in a throwaway worktree at
# head_sha, where negative_control.command must exit non-zero, then zero at a clean head_sha.
# REQUIRED whenever ORCA_NO_GH or ORCA_LIGHTING=dark-eligible is set. Name ORCA_BASE with it: the
# control restores files from base_sha, which must be a commit the integration branch holds.
# ORCA_EXECUTE_NC=

# Seconds the verifier may run before the gate stops it and BLOCKS (default 2100). Keep it below
# the host hook timeout (2400 in hooks/hooks.json): Claude Code discards a timed-out hook's output
# and lets the turn end, so an unbounded verifier would fail OPEN.
# ORCA_GATE_TIMEOUT_S=

# AUTHORITATIVE criterion-bound command the negative control must turn RED, supplied out of band the
# way the frozen contract is. The manifest's own negative_control.command must AGREE with it. There
# is no fallback (#279): with ORCA_EXECUTE_NC set and this unset, verify.py fails closed — a unit
# never nominates the command it is proved by.
# ORCA_NC_COMMAND=

# No-gh lane switch (same on/off spellings as ORCA_EXECUTE_NC): review authority becomes local
# review.artifact (a downgrade). Requires ORCA_EXECUTE_NC.
# ORCA_NO_GH=

# A | B | 0  (coordinator lane decision, forwarded as --lane)
# ORCA_UNIT_LANE=

# lit | dark-eligible  (coordinator lighting decision). dark-eligible requires ORCA_EXECUTE_NC.
# ORCA_LIGHTING=

# ci|mcp|sdk|dispatch  — asserts the env came from OFF the worker
# ORCA_PROVENANCE=

# Coordinator-signed dispatch envelope (path or path@ref)
# ORCA_DISPATCH_RECORD=

# Ed25519 verifying key, overriding key discovery. Trustworthy only when set off-worker. Without it
# the gate reads .orca/dispatch-pubkey from origin/HEAD, else from origin/<ORCA_BASE>; the working
# tree copy is read only on the advisory native lane (a worker writes that tree).
# ORCA_DISPATCH_PUBKEY=
